{
  "id": "P04",
  "format": "posting-scenario/v1",
  "name": "Service invoice of 10,000.0000 on credit, and the fences around the MVP variant",
  "rules": ["SALE_POSTED/service@1", "REPORT/trial-balance@1", "REPORT/account-ledger@1"],
  "source": "docs/posting-rules/service-sale.md",
  "governedBy": ["ADR-0005", "ADR-0011", "ADR-0014"],
  "executableFrom": "M3",
  "status": "Specified, hand-computed. Not yet executed: needs customers and sales invoices (M3). Steps 1-2 marked \"level\": \"kernel\" (Accounting seat ruling, 2026-09-29, review of the M3-Q throwaway verify against M3-P @efb7e3f): the real modules/receivables command has no lineNet/netAmount field for a client to submit — the module always computes them itself — so SALE_AMOUNT_MISMATCH is a kernel-only defense, reachable only by calling postingEngine directly, as P03 does. No figure changed.",
  "description": [
    "Line nets, computed by hand at the ONE rounding boundary (per line, half-up, 4 dp):",
    "  Line 1  1.000000 × 7500.000000 = 7500.000000  → 7500.0000",
    "  Line 2  3.000000 ×  833.333333 = 2499.999999  → 2500.0000",
    "          (truncation would give 2499.9999 — step 1 submits exactly that and is rejected)",
    "  netAmount = 7500.0000 + 2500.0000 = 10000.0000 (a sum of rounded values; not re-rounded)",
    "",
    "Entry:",
    "  Dr 1200 AR control [CUST-A]   10000.0000",
    "  Cr 4200 Service Revenue       10000.0000",
    "",
    "No residual can arise, so the rounding account stays at 0.0000.",
    "",
    "Steps 1–6 are rejections against separate draft invoices; none consumes an entry",
    "number or an invoice number, so step 7 receives JE-2027-000001 and INV-2027-000001."
  ],
  "fixture": {
    "coa": "standard-v1",
    "timezone": "Asia/Karachi",
    "fiscalYearStartMonth": 7,
    "today": "2026-09-27",
    "periods": { "fiscalYear": 2027, "status": "all OPEN" },
